package com.tamir.hamasa.ui.common

import android.graphics.Bitmap

/**
 * Measured crop rectangles of the badge and gear sprite sheets (res/drawable-nodpi badges_1..4, gear_1..4).
 *
 * The art is NOT on a uniform grid (badges drift up to ~30 px from the equal-cell lines, gear_4 sits in the
 * middle of its sheet), so a uniform crop showed coins off-centre with a sliver of the neighbour inside the frame
 * (e.g. "התיבה הראשונה", badges_3 index 4). These rectangles were generated by a PIL script from the alpha
 * channel: one seed per item (eroded opaque mask or XY-cut at the profile minima), every opaque pixel assigned to
 * its nearest seed, bounding box per item, shrunk until no pixel of another item is inside. gear_2 10/11 (the fox
 * and the winged helm drawn over each other) were set by hand from the contact sheet.
 *
 * Values are pixels of the ORIGINAL sheet ([NATIVE_W] x [NATIVE_H]); 4 ints per cell (left, top, right, bottom),
 * cells in the catalog's row-major index order. Scaled to the decoded bitmap (inSampleSize) at crop time.
 */
object SheetRects {
    const val NATIVE_W = 1600
    const val NATIVE_H = 893

    private val rects: Map<String, IntArray> = mapOf(
